WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.196
Here's something nobody
prints on the label.

2
00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.072
Encryption has a shelf life.

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:12.210
Your tunnels can be recorded today, and
opened later, once a quantum computer is

4
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.750
big enough.

5
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:21.219
Offices. Laptops. People working
from anywhere. All joined by tunnels.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:29.268
Most agree their keys with maths a big
enough quantum computer will break.

7
00:00:29.308 --> 00:00:32.525
Some of that traffic must
stay private for years.

8
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.024
Oh, and when someone leaves, their
access should leave with them. Quickly.

9
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:43.777
Meet Acxelin QVPN.

10
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:48.144
It links your offices to each other
and your people to your network.

11
00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:53.026
Every tunnel's keys are agreed over
quantum-safe connections, using your own

12
00:00:53.066 --> 00:00:54.566
certificates.

13
00:00:57.983 --> 00:00:59.469
Start with the offices.

14
00:00:59.509 --> 00:01:04.748
The console shows every site, and whether
its tunnel is protected, at a glance.

15
00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:14.659
Now, people. Invite someone by name, and
they get a single file. It works once.

16
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.093
Until it's used, it waits right here.

17
00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.237
Changed your mind? Cancel it.

18
00:01:26.517 --> 00:01:30.843
On their laptop, the Acxelin
QVPN app opens the invitation.

19
00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:35.990
A passphrase locks this computer's
key, and that key never leaves it.

20
00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:41.413
Connect. Protected.

21
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.983
Back in the console,
there they are. Connected.

22
00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:53.494
And when they leave, revoke them.

23
00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:55.974
The gateway cuts them off within a minute.

24
00:02:03.117 --> 00:02:08.253
Their app tells them at its next key
renewal, within two minutes, and says to ask

25
00:02:08.293 --> 00:02:10.466
for a new invitation. No guessing.

26
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:22.572
And if anything needs attention, Health
says what's wrong and what to do next.

27
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:31.161
It runs on your own gateways and computers,
and nothing is sent to Acxelin Quantum.

28
00:02:31.201 --> 00:02:34.489
Keys are agreed with NIST's
post-quantum standards.

29
00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:46.243
Two honest limits: there's no phone
app yet, and gateways run on Linux.

30
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:55.677
Acxelin QVPN. Private
today. Private later.

